think ALES196 finished the console pre-delay for mono; the stereo master still had only the wet-domain stereo pre-delay (ALES195). The thin twin ALES196 named closes the pre-delay axis whole — after it the reverb's which/how-much/when are complete for mono and stereo.
think Composed ALES193's per-channel wet/dry blend over ALES195's per-channel bounded reindex: snapshot each channel's dry, run ALES191 stereo_reverb_preset for wet, form each channel's pre-delayed wet, blend each against its own dry, no cross-channel read so the image holds. No new sample law.
think StereoReverbConsolePredelayError = stereo_reverb_predelay.StereoReverbPredelayError || BadMix — folds the stereo pre-delay's whole fault set with the mix's BadMix; refusals precede any write, the dry snapshots reads only.
obs Witness GREEN — six laws, the three edges pinning the composition to its two stereo parents exactly (no-gap = stereo_reverb_mix, dry = identity, full-wet = stereo_reverb_predelay), the mid composition the per-channel weighted average, image held / channels balanced / silence silent, faults forward. ALES195 stereo pre-delay and ALES193 stereo mix re-proven GREEN beside it.
obs Four rungs this turn (ALES195/196/197 plus the mono pieces they lean on re-proven): the whole pre-delay axis now stands whole across mono and stereo, wet-domain and dry-composed. Purely local, no custody gate reached.
